# PVGIS CSV Parsing Support

The goal is to enhance the `csv-spreadsheet-converter` application to correctly parse PVGIS CSV files, which contain metadata headers and empty lines before the actual data table.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The parser will automatically skip metadata lines in PVGIS files and use the `time,G(i)` row as the header. Metadata will be ignored for now, focusing on the tabular data.

## Proposed Changes

### CSV Spreadsheet Converter

#### [MODIFY] [script.js](file:///C:/Users/samsung/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/csv-spreadsheet-converter/script.js)
- Update [parseCSV](file:///C:/Users/samsung/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/csv-spreadsheet-converter/script.js#102-119) to detect and handle PVGIS-specific format.
- Implement logic to find the start of the data table.
- Filter out metadata and focus on the time-series data.

## Verification Plan

### Manual Verification
1. Open the updated [index.html](file:///C:/Users/samsung/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/solar-pv-calculator/index.html) in the browser.
2. Upload the PVGIS CSV data provided by the user (I will create a local [.csv](file:///C:/Users/samsung/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/csv-spreadsheet-converter/sample-data.csv) file with that data for testing).
3. Verify that the table displays rows starting from the data section (e.g., `20230101:0030`) and that the columns are correctly aligned under `time` and [G(i)](file:///C:/Users/samsung/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/solar-pv-calculator/pvgis-api.js#4-151).
4. Check that the row count and column count are correct for the tabular data.
